{
  "id": "KL_dhpvb-ZM",
  "segments": [
    {
      "start": 2.05,
      "end": 13.86,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "- And now there's Nazi's again.",
          "start": 2.05,
          "end": 4.26
        },
        {
          "text": "When I was a kid, Nazi's was just an analogy you would use to decimate your child during an argument at the dinner table.",
          "start": 7.09,
          "end": 13.86
        }
      ],
      "glossary": [
        {
          "term": "analogy",
          "ko": "비유, 빗댐",
          "type": "word"
        },
        {
          "term": "decimate",
          "ko": "박살내다, 완전히 짓밟다",
          "type": "word"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 17.37,
      "end": 22.53,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "There's new Nazi's.",
          "start": 17.37,
          "end": 18.7
        },
        {
          "text": "I don't care for these new Nazi's and you may quote me on that.",
          "start": 18.7,
          "end": 22.53
        }
      ],
      "glossary": [
        {
          "term": "don't care for",
          "ko": "좋아하지 않다, 마음에 안 들다",
          "type": "idiom"
        },
        {
          "term": "you may quote me on that",
          "ko": "그대로 인용해도 좋아 (확신의 표현)",
          "type": "idiom"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 23.92,
      "end": 32.59,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "These new Nazi's, oh Jews are the worst, and Jews ruin everything, and Jews try to take over your life.",
          "start": 23.92,
          "end": 30.57
        },
        {
          "text": "It's like, \"You know what, motherfucker?",
          "start": 30.57,
          "end": 32.59
        }
      ],
      "glossary": [
        {
          "term": "take over your life",
          "ko": "네 인생을 장악하다",
          "type": "phrase"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 32.59,
      "end": 37.86,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "My wife is Jewish.",
          "start": 32.59,
          "end": 34.87
        },
        {
          "text": "I know all that. (audience cheering) How do you know all that?\"",
          "start": 34.87,
          "end": 37.86
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 43.9,
      "end": 48.11,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "I'm allowed to make fun of my wife.",
          "start": 43.9,
          "end": 45.53
        },
        {
          "text": "I asked her, and she said yes.",
          "start": 45.53,
          "end": 48.11
        }
      ],
      "glossary": [
        {
          "term": "make fun of",
          "ko": "~을 놀리다, 조롱하다",
          "type": "idiom"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 49.79,
      "end": 61.24,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "I've been married for about three and a half years now, and I was going out on tour, (audience cheer) and, oh thank you very much, and I love and respect my wife very much.",
          "start": 49.79,
          "end": 58.43
        },
        {
          "text": "So I said to her, \"Hey, we've been married for three and a half years.\"",
          "start": 58.43,
          "end": 61.24
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 61.24,
      "end": 67.51,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "And she knew that.",
          "start": 61.24,
          "end": 62.14
        },
        {
          "text": "I said, \"Do you mind if I still make fun of you on stage?\"",
          "start": 63.39,
          "end": 67.51
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 67.51,
      "end": 81.75,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "And my wife said, she goes, \"Yeah, you can make fun of me, you can make fun of me, but just don't say that I'm a bitch and that you don't like me.\"",
          "start": 67.51,
          "end": 74.57
        },
        {
          "text": "I was like, \"Whoa, the bar is so much lower than I ever imagined, that's it?\"",
          "start": 74.57,
          "end": 81.75
        }
      ],
      "glossary": [
        {
          "term": "the bar is so much lower",
          "ko": "기준(눈높이)이 훨씬 낮다",
          "type": "idiom"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 82.84,
      "end": 89.98,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Also, I wouldn't say that, what kind of show would that even be?",
          "start": 82.84,
          "end": 86.35
        },
        {
          "text": "Hello, my wife is a bitch!",
          "start": 86.35,
          "end": 89.98
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 90.84,
      "end": 100.02,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "And I don't like her!",
          "start": 90.84,
          "end": 93.52
        },
        {
          "text": "That's like a support group for men in crisis, with keynote speakers Jon Voight and Alec Baldwin.",
          "start": 93.52,
          "end": 100.02
        }
      ],
      "glossary": [
        {
          "term": "support group",
          "ko": "(고민을 나누는) 자조 모임",
          "type": "phrase"
        },
        {
          "term": "men in crisis",
          "ko": "위기에 처한 남자들",
          "type": "phrase"
        },
        {
          "term": "keynote speakers",
          "ko": "기조 연설자들",
          "type": "phrase"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 103.11,
      "end": 108.7,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Also, I would never say that, not even as a joke, that my wife is a bitch and I don't like her.",
          "start": 103.11,
          "end": 107.55
        },
        {
          "text": "That is not true.",
          "start": 107.55,
          "end": 108.7
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 108.7,
      "end": 117.99,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "My wife is a bitch and I like her so much.",
          "start": 108.7,
          "end": 112.58
        },
        {
          "text": "She is a dynamite five foot Jewish bitch and she's the best.",
          "start": 113.46,
          "end": 117.99
        }
      ],
      "glossary": [
        {
          "term": "dynamite",
          "ko": "(속어) 끝내주는, 멋진",
          "type": "word"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 119.01,
      "end": 129.18,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "She and I have totally different styles.",
          "start": 119.01,
          "end": 121.47
        },
        {
          "text": "When my wife walks down the street, she does not give a shit what anyone thinks of her in any situation, she's my hero.",
          "start": 121.47,
          "end": 129.18
        }
      ],
      "glossary": [
        {
          "term": "does not give a shit",
          "ko": "전혀 신경 쓰지 않다 (비속어)",
          "type": "idiom"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 129.18,
      "end": 138.4,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "When I walk down the street, I need everybody, all day long, to like me so much.",
          "start": 129.18,
          "end": 135.54
        },
        {
          "text": "(audience laughing) It's exhausting.",
          "start": 135.54,
          "end": 138.4
        }
      ],
      "glossary": [
        {
          "term": "exhausting",
          "ko": "진을 빼는, 기진맥진하게 하는",
          "type": "word"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 138.4,
      "end": 150.52,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "My wife said that walking around with me is like walking around with someone who's running for mayor of nothing.",
          "start": 138.4,
          "end": 144.87
        },
        {
          "text": "My wife and I went to Best Buy to get a TV.",
          "start": 147.63,
          "end": 150.52
        }
      ],
      "glossary": [
        {
          "term": "running for mayor of nothing",
          "ko": "아무것도 아닌 시장 자리에 출마하는 (남의 눈을 의식한다는 농담)",
          "type": "phrase"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 150.52,
      "end": 159.17,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "We didn't end up getting the TV.",
          "start": 150.52,
          "end": 152.66
        },
        {
          "text": "I was afraid that the Best Buy guy was gonna be mad at me, so I bought an HDMI cable.",
          "start": 152.66,
          "end": 159.17
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 161.06,
      "end": 166.23,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "And I go up to the register with Anna, my wife's name's Anna, she's standing next to me.",
          "start": 161.06,
          "end": 164.4
        },
        {
          "text": "I hand the guy the HDMI cable.",
          "start": 164.4,
          "end": 166.23
        }
      ],
      "glossary": [
        {
          "term": "go up to the register",
          "ko": "계산대로 다가가다",
          "type": "phrase"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 166.23,
      "end": 172.83,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "He takes it, he scans it, and he says, \"Do you have a Best Buy rewards card?\"",
          "start": 166.23,
          "end": 169.96
        },
        {
          "text": "And I said, \"No, I wish.\"",
          "start": 169.96,
          "end": 172.83
        }
      ],
      "glossary": [
        {
          "term": "No, I wish",
          "ko": "아뇨, 그러면 좋겠지만요 (사실은 아님)",
          "type": "idiom"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 179.24,
      "end": 191.08,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "And then my wife said, \"Jesus Christ,\" and fully walked away from me.",
          "start": 179.24,
          "end": 185.06
        },
        {
          "text": "Walked all the way over to the laser printers and just stood there, Blair Witch style.",
          "start": 185.06,
          "end": 191.08
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 193.26,
      "end": 204.28,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "And I'm still up at the register like...",
          "start": 193.26,
          "end": 195.56
        },
        {
          "text": "And the guy goes, \"Do you want a Best Buy rewards card?\"",
          "start": 198.28,
          "end": 204.28
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 205.71,
      "end": 212.37,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "And I said, \"No.\"",
          "start": 205.71,
          "end": 207.96
        },
        {
          "text": "Even though I had just said it was my greatest wish in life.",
          "start": 209.11,
          "end": 212.37
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 212.37,
      "end": 226.18,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "I was hoping he'd believe me, that it was secretly my great wish, but that I'm in an abusive marriage with little miss Jesus Christ over here, so I can't ask for the things I want in public, but at home, at night, we argue about it.",
          "start": 212.37,
          "end": 224.73
        },
        {
          "text": "And I'm like, \"You'll see.",
          "start": 224.73,
          "end": 226.18
        }
      ],
      "glossary": [
        {
          "term": "abusive marriage",
          "ko": "학대받는 결혼 생활",
          "type": "phrase"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 226.18,
      "end": 234.05,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "One day I'm gonna leave you, and I'm gonna get that Best Buy rewards card.\"",
          "start": 226.18,
          "end": 231.68
        },
        {
          "text": "She's like, \"Jesus Christ.",
          "start": 231.68,
          "end": 234.05
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 236.16,
      "end": 242.97,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "You're never gonna get that Best Buy rewards card!\"",
          "start": 236.16,
          "end": 238.71
        },
        {
          "text": "My wife is Jewish, as I said.",
          "start": 241.14,
          "end": 242.97
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 242.97,
      "end": 249.09,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "I was raised Catholic.",
          "start": 242.97,
          "end": 244.29
        },
        {
          "text": "We have differences in our religious upbringings, and we realized this recently.",
          "start": 244.29,
          "end": 249.09
        }
      ],
      "glossary": [
        {
          "term": "raised Catholic",
          "ko": "가톨릭 집안에서 자란",
          "type": "phrase"
        },
        {
          "term": "religious upbringings",
          "ko": "종교적 양육 환경, 자라온 신앙 배경",
          "type": "phrase"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 249.09,
      "end": 253.62,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Not with our kids, 'cause we don't have any kids.",
          "start": 249.09,
          "end": 251.56
        },
        {
          "text": "People always ask us, \"Are you gonna have kids?\"",
          "start": 251.56,
          "end": 253.62
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 253.62,
      "end": 256.06,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "And we say, \"No.\"",
          "start": 253.62,
          "end": 254.73
        },
        {
          "text": "And then they go, \"Never?",
          "start": 254.73,
          "end": 256.06
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 256.06,
      "end": 259.51,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "You're never gonna have kids?\"",
          "start": 256.06,
          "end": 257.87
        },
        {
          "text": "Look, I don't know never.",
          "start": 257.87,
          "end": 259.51
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 259.51,
      "end": 266.59,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "14 years ago I smoked cocaine the night before my college graduation.",
          "start": 259.51,
          "end": 264.02
        },
        {
          "text": "Now I'm afraid to get a flu shot.",
          "start": 264.02,
          "end": 266.59
        }
      ],
      "glossary": [
        {
          "term": "flu shot",
          "ko": "독감 예방주사",
          "type": "phrase"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 266.59,
      "end": 268.15,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "People change.",
          "start": 266.59,
          "end": 268.15
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
